# Import UI design contract

- Before changes, read the latest business specification and inspect latest MagicPath OWNER/STAFF revisions in project 458079658328604672.
- Docs define behavior; MagicPath defines visual and interaction patterns. Do not invent final production screens.
- Map required states to explicit design states across the entire flow, including errors/recovery and permissions.
- Maintain docs/status/FOUND_MISSING_UI_V1.md as current truth; preserve docs/FOUND_MISSING_UI.md as historical evidence. Reuse existing FM IDs; classify distinct runtime/API/recovery debt separately without creating duplicate FM IDs.
- Separate missing design from FE/API/recovery/live/polish gaps; API availability or a CSS defect is not proof of missing design.
- Track Design/Frontend/Backend/Live verification independently, with owner, next action and safe behavior. Keep traceability when design arrives; fallback is not resolution.
- Share Owner/Staff Step 3 overview, focused resolver shell, footer and validation geometry. Role changes availability/transition, not layout.
- Retain business/API semantics, exact intents/CAS, source proof, atomic commit and independent Readiness. Never wire DESIGN_READY endpoints as runtime.
- Keep developer state controls DEV-only, outside layout; diagnostics secondary/collapsed.
- End each Import pass by reviewing the missing-design register and disclosing any bounded speculative production fallback.
